+<!-- CARROT:REVIEW reviewed-for="95f875649b5996bbd6d9c4beed3d700ca194799fc6dd5d79dcc111391559d318" reviewed-at="2026-11-10T00:00:00Z" -->
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+Porter II EV and Ioniq 5 HDA2 CAMERA SCC torque steering do not finish a navigation turn solely on falling predicted yaw. After steering exceeds 80 degrees in the turn direction, return within ±15 degrees for 0.2s while moving finishes it; an unchanged turn cue executes for at most 10s.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+Requires ATC mode 1 or 2 and active lateral control. Navigation changes, lateral disengagement and opposite physical turn-signal requests take priority; valid model output and fresh vehicle, control and navigation state are required; invalid CAN or steering angle stops retention.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+Maximum torque, rate and driver-override limits remain. A long turn may reach the time bound. This does not increase physical steering capacity or provide deceleration with cruise OFF.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
+
